  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Resilience of Crisis Affected Communities in South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project intends to improve the resilience of targeted crisis affected communities through improved food security, improving income and providing access to safe and adequate water supply services. The project targets host communities 75%, internally displaced persons 15% and returnee population 10%. At least 60% of the total households to be supported will be women headed households. Over 45 thousand people (21813 men and 23631 female) are targeted.</narrative>
  </description>
